# Code quality

## Change discipline

- Focused diff only — no drive-by refactors or unrelated formatting.
- Reuse and extend existing functions/components; do not reimplement parallel abstractions.
- No over-engineering: no one-line helpers, excessive error handling, or speculative edge cases.

## Backend (Spring Boot)

- Controllers thin; logic in `service/` or `grading/`.
- Upload/compile failures → `SubmissionProcessingException` (422 via `GlobalExceptionHandler`).
- New endpoints need CORS in `CorsConfig` when called from the SPA.
- Requires JDK (not JRE) for `JavaCompilerService`.

## Frontend (React + Vite)

- Pages in `src/pages/`; shared widgets in `src/components/`.
- Use semantic Tailwind tokens (`bg-primary`, `text-success`) — not raw `blue-600` or hex.
- Theme: edit `src/theme/tokens.js` and `src/theme/brand.js`; run `npm run theme:sync` after token edits.
- API errors: `src/utils/apiError.js` — friendly messages only, never raw backend `message`/`detail`.
- `fetch` + `API_BASE` pattern until a shared client exists.

## Tests

- No automated suite project-wide yet; add tests only when requested or they cover real behavior.
- Backend: `mvn test` from `backend/` when touching compile/submission paths.
- Frontend: `npm run build` must succeed.

## Review

- Subjective style nits without a project standard are not findings.
- Anchor review to `AGENTS.md` contracts and the actual diff scope.
